// Burrowers: segmented worms, eels and serpents. One row per strain.
// `kind` must also have a row in bestiary.ron (name, health, drops).
// Each spawned body rolls its own segment count, girth, weave and tint from a
// positional seed inside the ranges below, so two worms of one strain differ.
//
// motion:   Burrow  - swims through rock, arcs ballistically across open caves
//           Breach  - like Burrow, but leaps out of the ground in tall arcs
//           Slither - crawls along cave floors and walls like a snake
//           Swim    - stays inside water (or lava) and strikes at the surface
// hosts:    blocks the strain spawns inside or beside; the first match wins
//           against other strains by weight.
// ornament: Mandibles | Plates | Crystals | Caps | Frills | Spines
// trail:    Grit | Embers | Frost | Spores | Bubbles | Motes
// rumble:   camera tremor in metres when the head grinds rock at point blank.
// Optional hunter fields (Undercrown residents; live in every v2-layout world):
// district:   Some(index) - rises only inside that Undercrown district, one at a time
// patience_s: seconds of pursuit before it breaks off and withdraws (0 = never)
// rest_s:     seconds it stays at its lair after breaking off
// hears:      true - sense range scales with player speed; creeping slips it
// min_cover_m: metres of rock overhead needed where it rises (0 = anywhere); keeps
//             giants out of shallow ground and starter terrain
// tell_s:     seconds a lunge shows itself (dust at the player's feet, a groan)
//             before the head can hurt (default 1)
// Diggers (Burrow, Breach) never hunt a player standing under open sky unless
// wounded or touched; a lunge always shows its tell first.
[
    (
        kind: 80,
        motion: Burrow,
        hosts: [Stone, Limestone, Gravel, Clay, Dirt],
        weight: 1.0,
        segments: (10, 16),
        radius_m: (0.34, 0.55),
